{"seconds": 37.8, "exit": 0, "final": "The king can escape to g7. So the main winning line is: **Rc8!** forcing Rxc8, then **dxc8=Q+** and White has an overwhelming material advantage (a new queen).\n\nThis is a beautiful tactical blow. The key weakness was that Black's rook on d8 was undefended and pinned by White's d1 rook against Black's rook on d8. Rc8 forces the capture and the promotion.\n\n---\n\n**Best move:** Rc8\n\n**Main line:** Rc8 Rxc8 dxc8=Q+ Kg7 (or any king move)\n\n**Motif:** pin, promotion\n\n**Coaching note:**\nYour rook on d1 was eyeing d8 through your pawn on d7. Black's rook there was undefended\u2014a sitting duck. By advancing your rook to c8, you forced Black to capture, which allowed your pawn to promote with check. Always scan for undefended enemy pieces aligned with your pieces on open lines; they're often targets for forcing tactical blows.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rc8\", \"line\": [\"Rc8\", \"Rxc8\", \"dxc8=Q+\", \"Kg7\"], \"motifs\": [\"pin\", \"promotion\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30", "square": "d1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30", "square": "c5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30", "square": "d7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30", "square": "d8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r3k/r2P1p1p/6p1/p1R5/2p5/8/P4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 2 30", "move": "d8=Q"}},